  "about": "Every weapon the engine knows, by generic id. Weapons are data: a `warhead` (its row in the combat module's damage table) and tunable numbers. Distances are sub-tile units (256 per tile), times are ticks. `speed` 0 means an instant hit; otherwise a projectile flies that far each tick and lands within `scatter` of where it was aimed. `splash` is the blast radius: full damage within half of it, half damage within all of it. Our own numbers, from our own simulation runs.",
